  <prompt>
    Author the `compose-compare-to-playbook` capability as an Action row + Click-path Binding row (ADR-039), mirror-first under infra/dataverse/, dispatched through the shipped session-dispatch seam (NO new endpoint). The Action matches a selected clause against the matter/firm playbook clauses and returns `{matches: [{playbookEntryId, clauseText, deviations, riskScore, rationale}], overallRisk}` (FR-08). Critically, it READS existing `sprk_analysisplaybook` entries as reference data injected into the prompt — the playbook is NOT a routing target and NO new playbook is authored (engine frozen). Consumes the `compose-selection` JPS scope + matter context. Ships with eval cases in task 045.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    AI platform developer fluent in JPS Action authoring, the ADR-039 Action+Binding catalog model, playbook-as-reference-data consumption, and OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator constraints.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A deployable `compose-compare-to-playbook` Action row (SystemPrompt injecting the matter's playbook entries as reference context + OutputSchemaJson + Temperature + ModelDeploymentId) and its Click-path Binding row, authored mirror-first through the core's hoisted description source, consuming `compose-selection` + matter context, returning schema `{matches: [{playbookEntryId, clauseText, deviations, riskScore, rationale}], overallRisk: string}` passing OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator with no property-level boolean `required`. Zero new routes; eval-ready for task 045.
  </goal>

